<div id="about">
  <h2>About Me</h2>
  <p>
    I began my Computer Science degree at UC Santa Cruz in 2019 without a clear
    career direction. That changed in 2022 when I took a Full Stack Applications
    course, where I quickly picked up HTML, CSS, and JavaScript, and discovered
    a passion for building web apps. After graduating in 2023, I worked as a
    computer technician while developing side projects. Seeking larger impact, I
    joined Develop for Good, where I collaborated with a team to develop
    Concordia—an app coordinating aid efforts in the Dominican Republic.
    <br></br>
    Wanting to work on mission-driven, cutting-edge projects, I moved on to Tesla, where
    I currently work as an AP Engineer on the Optimus team.
    Supporting the development of autonomous robotics aligns with my passion for
    creating technology that solves meaningful, global challenges.
  </p>
